==============================================================================
Hoeffding threshold
==============================================================================
Hoeffding rule as coded (M=100, delta_total=0.5, T=30): p_diff in [0.0062, 0.0489] over n=1..18
  n= 4: [0.0132, 0.0245]
  n= 8: [0.0093, 0.0173]
  n=12: [0.0076, 0.0141]
  n=15: [0.0068, 0.0126]
  n=18: [0.0062, 0.0115]
sum_k delta_k with delta_k = delta_total/(T-k): 3.995 x delta_total = 2.00 for delta_total = 0.5

Derived rule: lock iff |P0hat - P1hat| >= tau = 2 sqrt(ln(2nT/delta)/(2M)), M = post-selected shots
post-selected shots M per iteration needed for tau = 0.01 (T = 30):
  delta=0.05  n=8: 1.83e+05   n=12: 1.91e+05   n=16: 1.97e+05   n=20: 2.02e+05
  delta=0.50  n=8: 1.37e+05   n=12: 1.45e+05   n=16: 1.51e+05   n=20: 1.56e+05

Statistical wrong-lock bound exp(-M tau^2/2) for an undecided qubit (D = 0), tau = 0.01:
  M=1e+03  bound 0.951
  M=1e+04  bound 0.607
  M=1e+05  bound 0.00674
  M=1e+06  bound 1.93e-22

Shots that give a marginal standard error equal to the rounding error 0.5*10^-d at P = 1/2:
  precision 3: M = 10^6
  precision 6: M = 10^12

